.TH I420 1
.SH NAME
i420 \- a video frame as a picture
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B i420
.I w h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I I420
reads one frame of
.I w
by
.I h
pixels in I420 (a plane of luma, then the half-size planes of blue and
red chroma, full-range BT.601: what
.IR camsrv (4),
vid9p and any feed of their schema serve) from its standard input, and
writes it as an uncompressed
.IR image (6)
picture, r8g8b8, on its standard output, for
.IR topng (1),
.IR tojpg (1)
or anything else that takes a picture. It knows nothing of where the
frame came from: a feed serves frames,
.IR read (1)
cuts one out, and the filters after it turn it into what is wanted.
.PP
A frame is
.IR w × h
bytes of luma and twice
.RI ( w +1)/2\(mu( h +1)/2
of chroma; a feed's
.B fmt
gives
.I w
and
.IR h .
.SH EXAMPLES
A still from a camera, as PNG and as JPEG:
.IP
.EX
read 189420 < /mnt/video/0/frame | i420 410 308 | topng > still.png
read 189420 < /mnt/video/0/frame | i420 410 308 | tojpg > still.jpg
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/i420.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR read (1),
.IR topng (1),
.IR camsrv (4),
.IR image (6)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A size not between 1 and 16384, or a frame shorter than the size
says, is refused, saying which.
